## Statement

Compute the remainder of $2^{100}$ when divided by $7$.

## Hint

Find the smallest $k$ with $2^k\equiv1\pmod7$.

## Solution

We have $2^3=8\equiv1\pmod7$. Since $100=3\cdot33+1$,
$$2^{100}=\left(2^3\right)^{33}\cdot2\equiv1^{33}\cdot2=2\pmod7.$$

The remainder is $2$.
